<title>AUSTRALIA: Qantas to lay off 185 workers - union.</title>
<headline>Qantas to lay off 185 workers - union.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qantas Airways Ltd had told unions it planned to lay off 185 workers from its engineering and maintainance division, the Australian Workers Union (AWU) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;They've said there's 185 going exactly and they are going from engineering and maintainace,&quot; AWU State Secretary Russ Collison told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said union officials had met with Qantas executives earlier on Tuesday to discuss the plans for the necessary cost cuts to increase competition.  </p>
<p>The 185 being laid off included 53 apprentices from the engineering and maintainance division.</p>
<p>Qantas is 25 percent by British Airways Plc.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
